From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:12:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] flash: the plugin lane takes the child's own surface (T-576)

While the lane is open RecvShow makes no copy: a movie's frame cost this thread up to 6.7 ms for a fresh surface and
a copy nobody read. The child's surface is the source, and the answer waits until the lane has taken it, so the
child stays off it and a card that cannot keep up holds the player at two frames in flight. RecvShow takes 83 us;
Bubble Tanks (55 fps) reaches 39.5 frames a second, against the stock browser's 32. The floor between draws, which
was for that overload, is gone: it cost the movies the card can keep up with their frames.

At the close the frame not taken, or the rows the card shows, become the layer's image. A plugin partly off the frame
keeps the copies (mode 1): its rows would not be there to go back to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
